Subject: [PATCH] C13's follow-ups, patch 4 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M29): THE TWELVE OLDER VERDICT LINES OF CLASS NEITHER CARRY A DATED NOTE ON
 THEIR PAGES, WAITING ON MAIN'S CHECK

C13's third follow-up classified the 115 older verdict lines that the gate selection-family reads; twelve are of class
"neither": a selection claimed with a value or a member as its object, whose page names neither the family it is made
from (a finite classification with a test of membership) nor a consistency condition, on the builder's reading. M29
asks for their dated notes now, marked as waiting on main's check of the classification's rows.

B44, B125, B266, B1154, B1228, B1230, B1235, B1258, B1298, B1406, B1806, B1857: at the end of each page, a dated note
that quotes the verdict line's own clause from the classification, says what the rule of 2026-11-12 asks, says that the
reading is the builder's and WAITS ON MAIN'S CHECK, and that the verdict, its numbers and the page's words are unchanged.
No verdict line is touched; no register row is added (one waits on main's check, as C13's README said).

THE LOCK, tests/test_the_twelve_selections_noted.py: the twelve are read from the classification itself, and held by the
digest of their list (the lock names no arc: the paper's verification manifest counts every lock that names an arc of
the paper, and this one is about none of its claims; the full suite found the count moved when it did); each page carries
the note once, with its clause in its words and its mark of waiting; no other page carries it. Planted: a note taken
out, a note without its mark of waiting, a note whose clause differs; each is reported alone.

